From 56a1fea496216a60d954d21343bcd15530cc804d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:16:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(trading): translate Bedrock merchant inventories in core

Open Java merchant screens from UpdateTrade, decode native NBT offers,
and submit selection, input placement, and result crafting through the
server-authoritative inventory request queue. Keep this in ViaBedrock
so direct connections and ViaProxy use the same implementation.

Preserve resolved costs separately from base prices, wildcard ingredient
damage, block states, result NBT, tiers, stock, and experience. Wait for
responses before subsequent transfers, restore rejected predictions,
and avoid double-counting stock when newer offers arrive first.

Native Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372, protocol 2193, confirms that
UpdateTrade alone opens the screen with Size=0 and trading-player=-1.
Its accepted requests use ingredient names 47/48 at slots 4/5 and
CreatedOutput slot 50 with the request ID. Hero of the Village confirms
buyA.Count is the resolved price and buyCountA is the base price.

Return trade inputs and the cursor before sending ContainerClose, as the
native client does. Serialize each return behind inventory responses so
new destination stack IDs are known before the next transfer. Closing
rejects further trade clicks; a full inventory drops only the overflow.
